([PROGRAM 2: Pure-Python Matrix Multiplier using List Comprehensions]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: Multiply two 2D matrices A \(m x k\) and B \(k x n\) using nested list) Tj
T*
(comprehensions without importing external libraries.) Tj
T*
(Python Source Code:) Tj
T*
(def matrix_multiply\(A, B\):) Tj
T*
(rows_A, cols_A = len\(A\), len\(A[0]\)) Tj
T*
(rows_B, cols_B = len\(B\), len\(B[0]\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(if cols_A != rows_B:) Tj
T*
(raise ValueError\(f'Incompatible shapes: \({rows_A}x{cols_A}\) and \({rows_B}x{cols_B}\)'\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(# Dot product: sum\(A[i][k] * B[k][j] for k in range\(cols_A\)\)) Tj
T*
(C = [[sum\(A[i][k] * B[k][j] for k in range\(cols_A\)\)) Tj
T*
(for j in range\(cols_B\)]) Tj
T*
(for i in range\(rows_A\)]) Tj
T*
(return C) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A = [[1, 2, 3],) Tj
T*
([4, 5, 6]]) Tj
T*
(B = [[7, 8],) Tj
T*
([9, 1],) Tj
T*
([2, 3]]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
